    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0b484518-e074-5bb0-9cd5-4973d766004d",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +7,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -7,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1+7 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +7\\le 1+7 \\\\ 6 & \\le x\\le 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $6\\le x\\le 8.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1-7 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -7\\le 1-7 \\\\ -8 & \\le y\\le -6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-8\\le y\\le -6.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $6\\le x\\le 8$ and $-8\\le y\\le -6.$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
