      ":question/id": "65ce124c-f583-52ba-a4eb-e40cfef66967",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1+4 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4\\le 1+4 \\\\ 3 & \\le x\\le 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $3\\le x\\le 5.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1\\le 1-1 \\\\ -2 & \\le y\\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-2\\le y\\le 0.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $3\\le x\\le 5$ and $-2\\le y\\le 0.$",
